---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Markly Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Markly link saving and bookmark application."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Markly Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Markly is a link saving and bookmark application designed to help you
          save, organize, manage, and return to content you discover across the web.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use
          Markly and the steps we take to respect and protect your privacy while
          you build and manage your saved collection.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Your Saved Links</h2>
        <p>
          The links and bookmarks you add to Markly are used to provide the core
          functionality of the application, including allowing you to save,
          organize, browse, and manage content you want to revisit.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your saved collection belongs to you. Markly does not sell your
          bookmarks, saved URLs, organizational information, or other content
          you create within the application.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Link Information</h2>
        <p>
          When you save a link, Markly may process information associated with
          that URL so the application can present useful details about the
          content you saved.
        </p>

        <p>
          Depending on the content available from the linked website, this may
          include information such as the page title, website name, URL,
          description, or other publicly available metadata associated with
          the saved page.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Third-Party Websites</h2>
        <p>
          Markly allows you to save links that lead to websites, services, and
          content operated by third parties. Those websites operate independently
          from Markly and may have their own privacy practices and policies.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you open a saved link and visit an external website, any information
          collected by that website is governed by the website's own privacy policy
          and is outside the control of Markly or Voxiverse.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Personal Information</h2>
        <p>
          Markly is designed around providing bookmark and link-management
          functionality rather than building advertising profiles about its users.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information processed through Markly is used only as necessary to
          operate, maintain, secure, and improve the application's features and
          the experience provided to you.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Markly does not sell your personal information or your saved-link
          activity to advertisers.
        </p>

        <p>
          Markly does not use your bookmark collection to create advertising
          profiles or track your browsing activity across unrelated third-party
          websites for advertising purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          Reasonable safeguards are used to protect information processed by
          Markly and to reduce the risk of unauthorized access, disclosure,
          alteration, or misuse.
        </p>

        <p>
          No electronic storage or transmission method can be guaranteed to be
          completely secure, but protecting the privacy and integrity of data
          associated with Markly remains an important part of how the application
          is maintained.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You can remove bookmarks and saved links from Markly when you no longer
          want them in your collection.
        </p>

        <p>
          Where additional user data or account-related information is retained
          by Markly, applicable deletion options and requests will be handled in
          accordance with the features and data-management options available
          through the application and Voxiverse.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Markly is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from
          children in violation of applicable privacy laws.
        </p>

        <p>
          If we become aware that personal information has been collected in a
          manner that requires parental consent or deletion under applicable law,
          appropriate steps will be taken to address that information.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy may occasionally be updated to reflect changes to
          Markly, new features, improvements, legal requirements, or changes to
          how information is processed.
        </p>

        <p>
          Updated versions will be published directly on this page with a revised
          last updated date so you can see when the policy has changed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how Markly handles
          information, you can contact Voxiverse:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>